{
  /* The web host's two dedicated Workers — the database's and the card scanner's — in a
     type-check program of their own, for the reason `infrastructure/relay/tsconfig.json` gives
     for the relay's: one program per runtime. (`packages/ui/lib/core/web/scanWorker.ts` is the
     second, since the light app's step 7.5: the same global scope, so the same program. What is
     said of `worker.ts` below is true of it, with `scanSession.ts`, `scanProtocol.ts` and
     `grimoire_scan.d.ts` as the modules followed from it.)

     `packages/ui/lib/core/web/worker.ts` runs in a dedicated Worker. It needs the `WebWorker`
     lib — `DedicatedWorkerGlobalScope`, a `postMessage` with no target origin — and the rest of
     `packages/ui/` has the `DOM` lib, which declares `self`, `postMessage` and `MessageEvent`
     over again and differently. In one program the two fight; `skipLibCheck` hides the fight
     inside the library files and leaves `self` typed as a `Window` in the one file where it is
     not one.

     So `packages/ui/tsconfig.json` **excludes** that file and this program holds it. The modules it
     imports — `engine.ts`, `protocol.ts`, `assets.ts` and the hand-written `grimoire_web.d.ts` —
     are followed from it and so are checked twice, once under each lib, which is the point: they
     are the half both sides read, and may name no global only one of them has.

     `vite/client` is listed for `import.meta.env`, which is how the Worker is told its engine's
     build id; this program does not contain `packages/ui/vite-env.d.ts`, whose triple-slash
     reference gives the app the same thing.

     This file sits in `packages/ui/` since 2026-10-08, beside the folder its two entries are
     under, and `include` is spelled from here.

     `pnpm build` and `pnpm web:build` both run it. */
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    /* No `DOM`: this is not a page. `ES2022.Error` for `tsconfig.base.json`'s reason. */
    "lib": ["ES2020", "ES2022.Error", "WebWorker"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "types": ["vite/client"],

    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["lib/core/web/worker.ts", "lib/core/web/scanWorker.ts"]
}
